            <ArticleTitle>[Complex treatment of vertebrogenic pain syndrome in women during pregnancy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The proposed system of non-pharmacological treatment has been tried in 325 pregnant women with pain syndrome associated with spinal lesions (osteochondrosis, scoliosis, malformations, sequela of compression vertebral fractures, spondylolisthesis). The treatment combined orthopedic aids, relaxing massage, muscular relaxation, mobilization of functional blocks of intervertebral joints and pelvic junctions, therapeutic exercises. The above non-pharmacological system relieved vertebral pain syndrome partially or completely in 82% of the treated pregnant women.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
